I find this project fascinating. The site will keep
growing slowly  in the following weeks. Course 1 should
be ready by July.

I appreciate your comments and feedback.

Today, I've introduced new sound recordings. The vowels are
somewhat shorter now in general and the "o" is different:
more like the Southern British English "lost", "got"
and "law". This should be the last major change though.

Lesson 1.2 ("coi" and "co'o") needs some exercises.
I'll add them sometime this week.

Be careful with lesson 1.3 because there is a vocabulary
problem! I've misinterpreted "nanmu" and "ninmu"...

I wonder how far I can go with this project without
explaining about Lojban grammar...

Martin


